  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer Ge/ZnS multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-bandpass transmission. Initialize all layer thicknesses using quarter-wave formula d_k = 4450nm/(4*n_k) where n_Ge≈4.0 and n_ZnS≈2.2 at 4.45μm center wavelength, giving initial Ge thickness ≈278nm and ZnS thickness ≈506nm. Set optimization bounds to ±40% around quarter-wave values (Ge: 167-389nm, ZnS: 304-708nm). Wavelength bands: transmit 4150-4350nm and 4550-4750nm, block 3600-4000nm and 4850-5200nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized. Max 24 layers constraint satisfied with 20 layers. No metal layers. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with coherent TMM across all bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 20-layer air | Ge | ZnS | ... | ZnS | CaF2 stack for dual-bandpass transmission at 4.15-4.35 µm and 4.55-4.75 µm while suppressing transmission in 3.60-4.00 µm and 4.85-5.20 µm. Initialize with quarter-wave thicknesses at 4.45 µm center, apply ±40% thickness optimization bounds, solve coherently at normal incidence.",
